### Configuring S3 Storage tiers
- It's nothing but assigning storage class to the objects
- Standard: frequently access data, >=3 AZs
- Intelligent-Tiering: Data with changing or unknown access patterns, >=3 AZs
- Standard-IA: Infrequently accessed data (once a month) with milliseconds access, >=3 AZs
- One Zone-IA: Recreatable, infrequently accessed data stored in single AZ with milliseconds access, 1 AZ
- Glacier Instant Retrieval: Long lived archive date accesses once a quarter, >=3 AZs
- aws s3 cp s3://budgets-east/2022/Budget1.txt s3://budgets-east/2022/Budget1.txt --storage-class GLACIER : Changes the storage class for an object through command

### Enabling S3 Object Lock
- Object lock feature can only be enabled while creating the new bucket only
- Using console we can't specify object lock for the objects, we have to use AWS CLI, SDK or S3 REST API
- these configurations applied to specific version of object 
- object lock legal hold is nothing but can't delete the version of file

