### AWS Storage Gateway
- Provides on-premises access to scalable cloud storage
- Use cloud storage locally with low network latency
- It supports cloud backup
- Existing services don't know they are talking to AWS resources

AWS Storage Gateway Deployment:
It can be deployed on 
- on-premises VM:
  - VMWare ESXi
  - Microsoft Hyper-V
  - Linux KVM
- EC2 instance
- Dedicated standalone physical hardware appliance

AWS Storage Gateway Types:
- S3 File Gateway
  - Local cache of files stores as S3 bucket objects
  - It allows on-premises access the content using SMB(used for windows) and NFS(used for Linux)
  - S3 data can be exposed to other AWS services like Amazon Athena
- FSx File Gateway
  - Files stored in S3 bucket in cloud shared as on-premises SMB file share and accessble through it
  - Since it appears as windows file share, it supports NTFS permissions and data deduplication 
- Tape Gateway
  - enables cloud backups
  - presents itself as an on-premises iSCSI virtual tape library (VTL)
  - stores virtual tapes in S3 and can be archived
- Volume Gateway
  - Presents itself as an on-premises block storage device through iSCSI
  - stores volume data in S3
  - Connects on-premises Linux and Windows servers to the volume using an iSCSI initiator

Deploy AWS Storage Gateway:
- Storage Gateway is applicance software or hardware based, it serves as a local file system cache for a variety of file offerings like tape library, shared folder or a disk volume. But in the end, storage is really backed in Amazon S3
