### S3 Bucket Encryption using the GUI
- Once bucket enabled with encryption, all the files that are going to upload post enablement encrypted automatically
- Existing files won't be encrypted

### S3 Bucket Encryption using the CLI
- aws s3 cp Project_D.txt s3://projects-east : existing encryption applied automatically
- aws s3 cp s3://projects-east/Project_E.txt s3://projects-east/Project_E.txt --sse AES256 : It enables encryption for file Project_E.txt though bucket level encryption is disabled.
- aws s3 cp Project_F.txt s3://projects-east --sse AES256 : enable encryption for file while adding itself.

### Content Delivery Netwroks (CDN)
- CDN serves as cache for requested information from web apps
- worldwide servers serve cached content to local users
- It reduces network latency, and improves app response time
AWS CloudFront
- User requests content via a URL of CDN server
- AWS maintains 410+ CDN servers globally
- It data is not cached on CDN, then CDN forwards request to origin server
- Data origin: S3, EC2, ELB, Media Services, API Gateway, on-premises data, HTTP Server
- CloudFront has enhanced media streaming capabilities, software patch deployment etc...
